  "about": [
    "Lacandon is a Mayan language of the Yucatecan branch, together with Yucatec Maya, Itza' and Mopan. About a thousand people speak it in the Lacandon Jungle of Chiapas: the northern Lacandon in Najá and Metzabok, the southern Lacandon in Lacanjá Chansayab.",
    "Its speakers call themselves jach winik, «true people», and their language jach t'aan, «the true language». The name Lacandon comes from an old Ch'ol town, Lakam Tun, «big stone».",
    "This page follows the southern variety recorded by Hofling. As in Mopan, the person is joined to the verb (kinbin «I go») and there is a sixth vowel, ä. The old l is pronounced r: kurtaar «sit down», 'ookar «go in»."
  ],
