    "intro": "We use the Mayan alphabet Hofling follows, with ts instead of tz: 6 vowels, which can be short, long or long with high tone (áa), and plain or glottalized consonants. The apostrophe (') marks a glottalized consonant (k', t') or a glottal stop; every word that starts with a vowel has a glottal stop: 'irik.",
